name: Will Acheson
email: will@arcex.app
Message: Subject: QuotaGuardShield Static IP not being applied to Prisma DB connections on Heroku

Technologies:
- NestJS v10.0.0
- Prisma v5.19.1
- Node.js v18.x
- QuotaGuardShield Plan shield Medium

Current Configuration:
- Heroku app with Procfile configured
- QuotaGuardShield addon installed and configured
- Supabase Postgres with IP restrictions enabled
- Allowed IPs: 3.251.32.127/32, 54.195.145.1/32

Steps Already Taken:
-  Configured proxy env vars to be used in both main.ts and PrismaService.
-  Configured Procfile with proxy settings
-  Set PRISMA_CLIENT_ENGINE_TYPE to binary
-  Added proxy settings to heroku-postbuild script
-  Verified successful build process
- Confirmed Supabase network restrictions include QuotaGuard IPs

Expected: All database connections routed through QuotaGuardShield static IP
Actual: Connections appear to be using dynamic Heroku IPs (e.g., {52, 211, 157, 81})

---
Hello,

I am working with a NestJS backend app running on Heroku that uses Prisma to connect to a Postgres database running on Supabase. 
I have set the quotaguardshield proxy URL set up in my .env file, but it doesnt seem to be being used during app deployment.  Our
app needs to be SOC 2 compliant so we have strict security enforced on our supabase db, meaning we restrict access to a designated
set of static IPs, so we need our heroku deployments to properly use the QuotaGuardShield proxy. 


I have made changes to my package.json file to include heroku-postinstall and heroku-postbuild commands that include setting the proxy urls as env vars, as well as setting the prisma client engine type to binary.  I've also modified by prisma service to set the proxy urls and additionally to my main.ts file.  

I now have my app building, which does not throw any errors (build logs included below), but after buliding and after my app starts, the app fails to connect to the db through prisma and throws this error:

```bash
2025-01-22T19:05:11.339867+00:00 app[web.1]: PrismaClientInitializationError: Error querying the database: FATAL: Address not in tenant allow_list: {52, 211, 157, 81}
2025-01-22T19:05:11.339868+00:00 app[web.1]: at Gr.<anonymous> (/app/node_modules/@prisma/client/runtime/binary.js:168:2956)
2025-01-22T19:05:11.339868+00:00 app[web.1]: at Gr.emit (node:events:517:28)
2025-01-22T19:05:11.339869+00:00 app[web.1]: at addChunk (node:internal/streams/readable:368:12)
2025-01-22T19:05:11.339869+00:00 app[web.1]: at readableAddChunk (node:internal/streams/readable:341:9)
2025-01-22T19:05:11.339869+00:00 app[web.1]: at Readable.push (node:internal/streams/readable:278:10)
2025-01-22T19:05:11.339869+00:00 app[web.1]: at Gr._pushBuffer (/app/node_modules/@prisma/client/runtime/binary.js:72:369)
2025-01-22T19:05:11.339869+00:00 app[web.1]: at Gr._transform (/app/node_modules/@prisma/client/runtime/binary.js:72:199)
2025-01-22T19:05:11.339870+00:00 app[web.1]: at Transform._write (node:internal/streams/transform:175:8)
2025-01-22T19:05:11.339870+00:00 app[web.1]: at writeOrBuffer (node:internal/streams/writable:392:12)
2025-01-22T19:05:11.339870+00:00 app[web.1]: at _write (node:internal/streams/writable:333:10) {
2025-01-22T19:05:11.339870+00:00 app[web.1]: clientVersion: '5.22.0',
2025-01-22T19:05:11.339871+00:00 app[web.1]: errorCode: undefined
2025-01-22T19:05:11.339871+00:00 app[web.1]: }
2025-01-22T19:05:11.339871+00:00 app[web.1]: 
```

The important part is the message about IP address not being in the tenant allow list. " Error querying the database: FATAL: Address not in tenant allow_list: {52, 211, 157, 81}". 

Upon subsequent deploys, this IP will change, meaning that at least this traffic is not being routed through the static IP proxy.  

Heroku Build Logs:

```bash
-----> Build
       Detected both "build" and "heroku-postbuild" scripts
       Running heroku-postbuild

       > arcex-backend@0.0.1 heroku-postbuild
       > npm run build && PRISMA_CLIENT_ENGINE_TYPE=binary http_proxy=$QUOTAGUARDSHIELD_URL https_proxy=$QUOTAGUARDSHIELD_URL prisma generate && prisma migrate deploy


       > arcex-backend@0.0.1 build
       > nest build

       Prisma schema loaded from prisma/schema.prisma

       ✔ Generated Prisma Client (v5.22.0, engine=binary) to ./node_modules/@prisma/client in 167ms

       Start by importing your Prisma Client (See: https://pris.ly/d/importing-client)

       Help us improve the Prisma ORM for everyone. Share your feedback in a short 2-min survey: https://pris.ly/orm/survey/release-5-22

       Prisma schema loaded from prisma/schema.prisma
       Datasource "db": PostgreSQL database "postgres", schema "public" at "aws-0-ap-northeast-1.pooler.supabase.com:5432"

       28 migrations found in prisma/migrations


       No pending migrations to apply.
┌───────────────────────────────────────────

...
-----> Build succeeded!
-----> Discovering process types
       Procfile declares types -> web
-----> Compressing...
       Done: 113M
-----> Launching...
       Released v28
       https://arcex-backend-1-aedcf684305a.herokuapp.com/ deployed to Heroku

```

Here is my PrismaService: 

```typescript
import { Injectable, OnModuleInit } from '@nestjs/common';
import { PrismaClient } from '@prisma/client';
import { URL } from 'url';

@Injectable()
export class PrismaService extends PrismaClient implements OnModuleInit {
    constructor() {
        const db = new URL(process.env.POSTGRES_PRISMA_URL);

        // quotaguard url 
        const proxyURL = process.env.QUOTAGUARDSHIELD_URL;

        if (proxyURL) {
            process.env.http_proxy = proxyURL;
            process.env.https_proxy = proxyURL;
            super({
                datasources: {
                    db: {
                        url: process.env.POSTGRES_PRISMA_URL,
                    },
                },
            });
        } else {
              // for running locally / outside of heroku
            super({
                datasources: {
                    db: {
                        url: process.env.POSTGRES_PRISMA_URL,
                    },
                },
            });
        }
    }
    async onModuleInit() {
        await this.$connect();
    }
    async onModuleDestroy() {
        await this.$disconnect();
      }
}
```

And here is my main.ts file: 

```typescript
if (process.env.QUOTAGUARDSHIELD_URL) {
  process.env.PRISMA_CLIENT_ENGINE_TYPE = 'binary';
  process.env.http_proxy = process.env.QUOTAGUARDSHIELD_URL;
  process.env.https_proxy = process.env.QUOTAGUARDSHIELD_URL;
}

import { NestFactory } from '@nestjs/core';
import { AppModule } from './app.module';

async function bootstrap() {
  const app = await NestFactory.create(AppModule);
  // Use Heroku-provided port or fallback to 3000
  const port = process.env.PORT || 3000;

  app.enableCors();
  await app.listen(port);
}
bootstrap();

```

Here is my supabase network restrictions, which include my two QuotaGuard static IPs (3.251.32.127 and 54.195.145.1):

```bash
$ supabase network-restrictions --project-ref xxxxxxxx get --experimental
DB Allowed IPv4 CIDRs: &[3.251.32.127/32 54.195.145.1/32 136.62.118.152/32 52.4.240.197/32]
DB Allowed IPv6 CIDRs: &[]
Restrictions applied successfully: true
```

Here is my Heroku Procfile: 
```procfile
web: PRISMA_CLIENT_ENGINE_TYPE=binary http_proxy=$QUOTAGUARDSHIELD_URL https_proxy=$QUOTAGUARDSHIELD_URL npm run start:prod
```

Here is my QuotaGuardShield URL (sans pw):
```
QUOTAGUARDSHIELD_URL=https://naiazcswxcey7f:xxxxxxxxx@eu-west-shield-02.quotaguard.com:9294
```

Please let me know if there are any little tricks or anything I might have missed in order to get my app to properly use the static IP proxy.  

Is there a specific configuration required for Prisma to use QuotaGuardShield?

Are there any known issues with Prisma's connection pooling and proxy usage?

Should the proxy configuration be handled differently for the Prisma Client vs the Prisma Engine?

Is there any additional configuration needed in the Prisma schema itself to ensure proxy usage?

Let me know if there is any other details you need from me as well, I am available via email or text message or even a call if needed.

Thank you kindly! 

Will Acheson
914-484-0047 (available 10am-7pm CST)
CTO @ Arcex 
Arcex.app


