Hello,

I started using QuotaGuard but running into an issue with SOCKS5

I white listed the IP’s given, but after a few hours of testing and getting no where I disabled my firewall to see an IP connection coming from a different IP that what’s listed below - 44.210.245.40

1) I’d like to confirm that’s one of your IP’s and I didn’t completely jack something up and it’s totally bypassing QuotaGuard.
2) If it is one of yours … how? Did I miss some step that’s needed to make sure I’m using my IP’s?

I’m not tunneling. That looked more complicated (at least to get started) and I do not need end to end encryption. I’m just using url: SOCKS5 URL socks5://**user**:**pass**@us-east-static-10.quotaguard.com:1080

Then in my node.js app I’m using it this way:


import { SocksProxyAgent } from "socks-proxy-agent";

export async function runRequest(
  requestData: string | Uint8Array,
): Promise<StandardizedRate[]> {
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    const proxyUrl = process.env.QUOTAGUARDSTATIC_URL;
    if (!proxyUrl) {
      reject(new Error("QUOTAGUARDSTATIC_URL is not defined"));
      return;
    }

    const agent = new SocksProxyAgent(proxyUrl);

    const options = {
      host: "67.225.172.254",
      port: 2000,
      agent: agent,
    };

    const client = net.connect(options, () => {
      console.log("Connected to server");
      client.write(requestData);
    });

    let data = "";

    client.on("data", (chunk) => {
      data += chunk;
    });

    client.on("end", () => {
      console.log("Received: ", data);
      try {
        const parsedResponse = parseFedExResponse(data);
        resolve(parsedResponse);
      } catch (error) {
        reject(error);
      }
    });

    client.on("error", (err) => {
      console.error("Request error: ", err);
      reject(err);
    });

    client.on("timeout", () => {
      console.error("Request timeout");
      client.end();
      reject(new Error("Request timeout"));
    });

    client.setTimeout(10000); // Set timeout
  });
}

Best Regards,
Wayne Dryden
225-588-9117


