Hi There,



I am trying to use QuotaGuard to allow my Heroku app to connect to MongoDB.
I have whitelisted the QuotaGuard static IP addresses that I was provided
in MongoDB but I am still having a failure with connecting to MongoDB via
QuotaGuard from my app. My app is nodejs with Typescript.



I have taken the following steps:

   - Downloaded qgtunnel from portal in /bin directory
   - Updated my index.ts to initialize global tunnel:

// Initialize global-tunnel-ng if QUOTAGUARDSTATIC_URL is provided

if (process.env.QUOTAGUARDSTATIC_URL) {

  globalTunnel.initialize({

    host: process.env.PROXY_HOST as string,

    port: parseInt(process.env.PROXY_PORT as string, 10),

    protocol: 'https:' || 'http:',

    connect: 'both'

  })

}

   - Updated my MongoDB connection to pass proxy params: I pulled proxy
   param details from the QUOTAGUARDSTATIC_URL

// Build the MongoDB connection string with proxy details

const buildMongoConnectionString = (): string => {

  const mongoUri = process.env.MONGO as string

